# Constitution Governance

Before writing ANY code in this project, you MUST:

1. **Read `AGENTS.md`** in the repo root. It is the project constitution (single source of truth; `gemini.md` is a legacy alias that `@`-imports it).
2. **Follow ALL rules** defined there. They override your default behavior.
3. **Check `.cursor/rules/`** for fine-grained, glob-scoped policies.
4. **Never violate modularity.** Do not add logic to `main.py` or `App.tsx`. Extract to modules.
5. **Never violate file size limits.** No file > 400 lines for new code.
6. **Log your work.** Update `CHANGELOG.md` for every behavior change; **MUST** prepend `PROBLEM_LOG.md` after any bug fix / diagnosis (mandatory for every agent -- see `problem-log.mdc`); **MUST** run `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py status` **before any fix**, and open or update a GitHub Issue labeled `deferred` after parking a known bug or feature (see `deferred-log.mdc`); write the task narrative in the PR body (`.github/pull_request_template.md`), or under `knowledge/task-log/` when there is no PR (see `task-log.mdc`).
7. **PR-first delivery** for every code/config/CI/security/rule task. **Clean start:** `git fetch origin`, then a NEW focused branch from `origin/master` only. Do not start on a dirty local/desktop worktree or another feature branch unless the user explicitly names that branch. **Finish:** verify, commit, push, and open a ready (non-draft) PR. The PR URL is the finish line -- do not end with local-only or unpushed commits. Casual phrasing ("quick fix", "just tweak") does not waive this. GitHub Actions merges it when CI is green (`github-delivery.mdc` item 10). Do not wait for the human to say merge. Direct `master` pushes require status-only scope or explicit user instruction. After the PR is merged or closed, **delete the head branch** (`github-delivery.mdc` item 8). Put every actionable issue on [Nova Delivery](https://github.com/users/aaltaay/projects/1) when the token allows (`gh project item-add 1 --owner aaltaay --url ...`); on 403 report the limitation instead of claiming the item exists.

## Rule Hierarchy (highest to lowest)

1. `AGENTS.md` — Project Constitution (supreme law; `gemini.md` aliases it)
2. `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — Fine-grained enforcement policies
3. Agent system prompts — Default AI behavior (overridden by above)

## Quick Reference: Common Violations to Avoid

- ❌ Adding a function to `backend/main.py` → put it in the correct module
- ❌ Adding a component to `frontend/src/App.tsx` → put it in `components/`
- ❌ Hardcoding a number or string → put it in `constants.py` / `constants.ts`
- ❌ Direct-pushing product work to `master` -- use a focused branch and PR
- ❌ Starting edits on a dirty worktree or a stale local `master` -- fetch and branch from `origin/master`
- ❌ Ending a coding session with local-only commits, unpushed commits, or "I'll open the PR later"
- ❌ Parking a shippable PR as draft because CI is still running
- ❌ Leaving a shippable PR open and idle -- Actions merges ready PRs; do not wait for "please merge"
- ❌ Leaving a merged or closed PR's head branch on origin -- delete it in the same session
- ❌ Claiming an issue is on Nova Delivery after a 403 / missing `project` scope -- report the limitation; do not recreate https://github.com/users/aaltaay/projects/1
- ❌ Forgetting CHANGELOG.md → entry required for every behavior change
- ❌ Fixing a bug without a `PROBLEM_LOG.md` entry → mandatory for every agent
- ❌ Parking a known bug or feature without a GitHub Issue labeled `deferred` → dump in agent-memory Backlog is not enough
- ❌ Starting a fix that is already an open `deferred` issue without reading that issue first
- ❌ Swallowing an error silently → log it, fix root cause, update PROBLEM_LOG.md

## Context economy

- Do not re-read files already provided in this session's context.
- Prefer Grep/Glob over reading whole files longer than ~400 lines.
- Cite code references instead of pasting file contents into replies.
